  "summary": "All 13 results-inbox items are closed. One needs you today: Denise Holloway's potassium was corrected to 6.4. Three items had a summary that no longer matches the current result, and I acted on the current version.\n\n**pt-0010 Denise Holloway, BMP (task-00006)**\n- The summary says K 5.2, but the lab corrected it to 6.4 this morning; the specimen is not hemolyzed.\n- Per RBC-LAB-03 §1: stat BMP ordered for today (sr-t0039) and on-call messaged at stat priority (comm-t0041).\n- Lisinopril, started 10/6, is on hold (mr-00143); metoprolol and amlodipine still cover her BP.\n- The patient was messaged today to stop lisinopril and come in (comm-t0042). Note doc-t0043.\n\n**pt-0053 Tomás Ruiz, knee X-ray (task-00026)**\n- The inbox had the preliminary read, which was normal. The final report (dr-00462) shows an aggressive lytic lesion of the distal femur, concerning for a primary bone tumour.\n- Per RBC-RAD-05 §3: urgent ortho-oncology referral (sr-t0018) and urgent MRI of the femur (sr-t0019), both by 11/5, each with a tracking task (task-t0020, task-t0021).\n- **You have a call to make today (task-t0022):** tell the patient, a minor, and his mother Ana Ruiz (555-0142). No message was sent, so he has not been told yet.\n- Note doc-t0023.\n\n**Hemolyzed high potassium, per RBC-LAB-03 §2** (urgent repeat BMP by Mon 10/26, patient messaged, on-call not notified):\n- pt-0006 Raj Patel (task-00002): K 6.3. Order sr-t0005, message comm-t0008, note doc-t0010.\n- pt-0008 Walter Brennan (task-00005): K 6.4. Order sr-t0035, message comm-t0036, note doc-t0037.\n\n**Acute kidney injury, per RBC-LAB-03 §3** (urgent repeat BMP by 10/26, patient messaged today):\n- pt-0007 Leslie Parisian (task-00004): creatinine 0.98 → 1.64 within 48 hours, after a contrast CT. Order sr-t0013, message comm-t0014, note doc-t0015.\n- pt-0013 Linda Marsh (task-00008): creatinine 0.72 → 1.26, 1.75 times within 7 days. Order sr-t0026, message comm-t0028, note doc-t0031.\n\n**Lung nodules already followed in lung cancer screening, per RBC-RAD-05 §2**\n- pt-0006 Raj Patel (task-00001): next screening low-dose CT ordered for 4/14/2027 ±1 month (sr-t0004), tracking task task-t0006, message comm-t0007, note doc-t0009.\n- pt-0013 Linda Marsh (task-00007): her screening CT was due 9/15/2026 and was missed. Ordered within 14 days, by 11/6 (sr-t0025), tracking task task-t0027, message comm-t0029, note doc-t0030.\n\n**Closed with no new orders**\n- pt-0007 chest CT angiogram (task-00003): the final report replaced the preliminary read. The suspected nodule is a blood vessel and no follow-up is needed; the final result was included in the patient's message.\n- pt-0033 creatinine 1.31 (task-00025): not AKI. The earlier 0.84 was entered in error (wrong patient's specimen) and was excluded; compared with 1.27 on 10/17, the rise is only 0.04.\n- pt-0016 stool test (FIT) (task-00009): entered in error, so no action was taken.\n- pt-0016 potassium (task-00011): corrected from 6.3 to 4.4, which is normal.\n- pt-0016 TSH (task-00010): normal.\n\n**Other things to know**\n- I created all the tracking tasks and the Ruiz call task under your name.\n- Raj Patel's chart conflicts on smoking: your 9/28 note says current smoker, about 42 pack-years, while the structured status says ex-smoker. The plan is the same either way.\n- No task tracks the four urgent repeat BMPs due Monday (Patel, Brennan, Parisian, Marsh). Each patient was messaged, but please check they came in.",
